Article 4 (Duties)
(1) To ensure safety and maintain order in the premises, security management personnel shall perform the following duties under the direction and supervision of the overall officer in charge:
1. Verifying the purpose of visits by persons and vehicles seeking entry into the premises;
2. Verifying the identities of persons entering the premises by means of resident registration cards or other identity documents, issuing entry passes, and confirming that such passes are worn on the premises;
3. Inspecting the possessions of entrants using metal detectors, X-ray screening equipment or other baggage inspection equipment to determine whether they possess weapons, other dangerous objects or objects interfering with order on the premises (hereinafter referred to as "dangerous objects, etc.");
4. Temporarily storing dangerous objects, etc. carried by entrants, requiring their removal from the premises, or reporting them to, or requesting cooperation from, a police agency;
5. Restricting entry to or requiring the departure of the following persons:
(a) Persons possessing dangerous objects, etc.;
(b) Persons who have harmed or intend to harm another person's life, body or property, etc.;
(c) Persons who have obstructed or intend to obstruct the duties of election commission public officials;
(d) Persons who have disturbed or intend to disturb peace and order on the premises;
(e) Persons who repeatedly fail to comply with requests for cooperation or measures taken by security management personnel and for whom restrictions on entry or removal are deemed necessary;
6. Controlling parking within the premises;
7. Checking for hazards through patrols or CCTV monitoring within the premises;
8. Other duties prescribed by the head of the establishing agency.
(2) In performing duties under paragraph (1), security management personnel may take minimum measures necessary for restraint or use protective equipment, including portable video recording equipment.
(3) In an emergency requiring protection of life, body or property, or maintenance of order, security management personnel may take necessary measures, including using portable video recording equipment, without awaiting instructions from the overall officer in charge. In such cases, they shall report the matter to the overall officer in charge without delay.
(4) In performing duties under paragraphs (1) through (3), security management personnel shall take care not to infringe the personal dignity or honor of persons entering the premises.
